WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.150
I've said before that voting Donald Trump
out is only the beginning.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.740
And the analogy I used was that for the last
three and a half years, we've essentially

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:11.740
been playing defense.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:12.740
We haven't had the ball.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.619
We've been trying to get the ball back.

00:00:14.619 --> 00:00:20.820
If Donald Trump is removed by Joe Biden and
becomes the next president and Joe Biden becomes

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.290
the next president, we haven't scored.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.180
We've just gotten the ball back.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.550
And that's when the fight will will really
begin.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:32.860
And it's important to flush this out a little
bit now because we're now only four months

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.430
from the election.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.980
Donald Trump is becoming increasingly unhinged.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:42.270
There's really two ways in which voting Trump
out will only be the beginning.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:47.360
Trump out as she achieves no progressive policy
like just removing Trump doesn't give progressives

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.360
any kind of policy victory.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.390
We will only get progressive policy done if
and when Trump leaves.

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:54.920
If we demand it from whoever is

00:00:54.920 --> 00:01:00.580
the next president, be it Joe Biden or be
it someone else in 2024.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:06.820
The removal of Trump is the start of the possibility
of progressive policy change.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.430
But it's not actually any policy change.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.630
So in that sense, getting Trump out is only
the beginning.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.730
And I've talked about that before.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.460
But there's another side to this which is
really ugly.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:20.700
And we have to sort of come to terms with
even if you remove Donald Trump, you've not

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:26.409
removed Trump ism. Trump ism is a virus that
is going to be around for a while.

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:30.350
And by Trump ism, I'm talking about all of
the really ugly stuff that we've seen for

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:35.250
years now, the legacy of nepotism and corruption
and the normalization of that in government.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:40.830
The mainstreaming of racism and xenophobia
that existed before Trump, but it wasn't so

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.549
brazenly out in public.

00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:43.549
That's one of

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:48.130
the things that Trump has done, is coalesced
and sort of said to the xenophobes and racists,

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.270
come back out into the public, come back out.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:51.270
You're welcome.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:56.850
Now, a ton of the behavior that people felt
ashamed about before and would keep behind

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.100
closed doors.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.400
Now it's become almost glorified in some sense.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.220
That won't go away the day Trump is removed.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:08.220
The coarsening of language, as I call it,
you know, grab him by the You-Know-What, making

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.470
fun of people with disabilities, tweeting
white power videos.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:13.450
I could go on and on and on with dozens of
examples.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:16.880
That's not going to go away when Donald Trump
leaves office.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.300
And in fact, it could actually get worse if
Donald Trump loses and claims that it was

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.470
rigged.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:29.550
We might see the absolute worst of it come
out with guns to protest an election that

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.870
Donald Trump may use

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:35.819
to convince his followers that it was actually
rigged against him.

00:02:35.819 --> 00:02:41.960
So if we see that type of violence, it could
get worse before it actually gets better.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.099
And then what about Republicans?

00:02:44.099 --> 00:02:49.349
We also have to deal with the Republicans
in the House and Senate who have been gleefully

00:02:49.349 --> 00:02:51.790
cheering Trump, some of them.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:56.220
Others have stood aside and allowed Trump
ism to take hold and run rampant.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:00.430
I'm thinking of people like Susan Collins,
who's perpetually, perpetually disappointed

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:03.099
with Trump but doesn't actually do anything
about it.

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:06.970
And arguably, the enablers are just as bad
as the cheerleaders.

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:11.000
None of that will be removed just because
Donald Trump is removed in November.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.870
So the point here is not to put the cart before
the horse and pretend Biden's got this thing

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:15.870
in the bag.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:17.170
We have won nothing yet.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.810
We're still trying to get the ball back by

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:22.710
removing Donald Trump in November.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:25.300
If and when that happens, it could be this
November.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.159
It could be November of 2024.

00:03:27.159 --> 00:03:29.750
That Trump leaves, first of all.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:34.340
We may have to bear the brunt of a short period
of even more chaos and violence in the streets

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:37.830
from people who will simply refuse to believe
that Donald Trump lost.

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.470
If, indeed, he loses in November.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:41.480
But then we've got to look at the Senate.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.750
We have to look at the House, we have to look
at governors, and we have to look at the culture

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:45.970
that has been created.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:47.519
The culture of Trump ism.

00:03:47.519 --> 00:03:52.850
And this is why I keep talking about we get
to vote in multiple elections in November.

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:54.409
We get to vote for Joe Biden.

00:03:54.409 --> 00:03:59.060
But if you're in Arizona, you also get to
vote for Mark Kelly to replace Martha McSally.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.220
If you're in Montana, you

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:05.330
get to vote for Joe Biden, but you also can
vote for Steve Bullock to be elected senator.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.260
Amy McGrath in Kentucky.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:12.870
All of these other options where we can replace
senators who have either been actually supporting

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.560
Trump or standing aside and not getting in
Trump's way.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.249
They are all part of the problem.

00:04:18.249 --> 00:04:23.879
And then when you look at specific issues,
you really I mean, it's hard not to be pessimistic.

00:04:23.879 --> 00:04:25.669
You realize what we are up against.

00:04:25.669 --> 00:04:30.869
If we remove Trump in November, we will have
lost four years.

00:04:30.869 --> 00:04:35.949
When it comes to the environment and the climate,
we can't get those years back.

00:04:35.949 --> 00:04:41.189
And so what that means is that we're going
to have to go above and beyond even what we

00:04:41.189 --> 00:04:46.559
thought we would have to deal with to handle
the destruction that Donald Trump has done.

00:04:46.559 --> 00:04:49.770
And I will go even further if even

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:56.520
if Joe Biden defeats Donald Trump in November,
we are going to have Trump's type candidates,

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:57.779
at least in 2022.

00:04:57.779 --> 00:05:02.099
Try to get in, possibly in 2024.

00:05:02.099 --> 00:05:07.660
So we're going to have multiple election cycles
during which we will have to resist these

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:13.749
malignancies so that we can try to end the
national nightmare that is Trump ism.

00:05:13.749 --> 00:05:17.779
So, again, let's not put the cart before the
horse.

00:05:17.779 --> 00:05:24.379
Your job is to envision that when you go to
vote in November, your vote could be the difference

00:05:24.379 --> 00:05:28.319
maker between Trump wins your state and Biden
wins your state.

00:05:28.319 --> 00:05:31.159
Mathematically, it's very unlikely to come
down to one vote.

00:05:31.159 --> 00:05:34.659
But if we all have that mentality, none of
us will stay home.

00:05:34.659 --> 00:05:35.969
We will all go out and vote.

00:05:35.969 --> 00:05:36.969
That's number one.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.509
We don't put the cart before the horse.

00:05:38.509 --> 00:05:41.439
But remember that you might also be voting
on a Senate

00:05:41.439 --> 00:05:42.559
race.

00:05:42.559 --> 00:05:48.509
And if the right thing were to happen in November,
then and only then will we be able to say

00:05:48.509 --> 00:05:50.240
now the work starts now.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:55.949
We spend the transition period figuring out
how will we make Biden as left as possible?

00:05:55.949 --> 00:05:59.249
How will we hold Biden accountable to the
concessions?

00:05:59.249 --> 00:06:04.809
And there have been some that he's made to
the more progressive wing of the Democratic

00:06:04.809 --> 00:06:05.809
Party.

00:06:05.809 --> 00:06:06.809
That's where it all starts.

00:06:06.809 --> 00:06:08.809
And it's going to be a very, very long battle.

00:06:08.809 --> 00:06:13.589
So, you know, last week or the week before,
I got a phone call from a viewer saying, you

00:06:13.589 --> 00:06:15.889
know, isn't the Senate really more important?

00:06:15.889 --> 00:06:20.800
Because even if we remove Biden, but we don't
have the Senate, we can't do that much.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:25.169
It's all important we get to vote for president
and we get to vote for senator in some states

00:06:25.169 --> 00:06:27.080
at 35 races.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.080
And we

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.080
get to vote for House of Representatives.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:33.030
And some governors and some state reps and
states that it all matters.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.289
It's not one or the other.

00:06:34.289 --> 00:06:39.599
It's we should all participate and we are
going to have to resist this viral virus of

00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:47.490
Trump ism, not only at every level in November,
but likely for a few election cycles to come.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:52.749
And that is why I we just have to keep the
pressure up on all aspects of this.

00:06:52.749 --> 00:06:56.610
We have to keep the pressure up from the perspective
of voter suppression.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:07:01.039
We have to keep the pressure up when it comes
to the TV ads.

00:07:01.039 --> 00:07:04.550
We have to keep the pressure up when with
these other online groups that are putting

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.439
together really good videos targeting Trump.

00:07:06.439 --> 00:07:10.719
We don't know what it is that will make a
difference when we look back at 2016.

00:07:10.719 --> 00:07:12.770
Was it Combs's second press

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:14.770
briefing about Hillary?

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:17.819
Was it Russian social media campaigns?

00:07:17.819 --> 00:07:22.310
Was it Hillary not visiting Wisconsin towards
the end of the day?

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:24.270
You will never know the one thing.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:29.589
And when you have such a complex election
with 300 in a country of 330 million, but

00:07:29.589 --> 00:07:34.479
one hundred and twenty hundred and thirty
million votes, no one thing is ever going

00:07:34.479 --> 00:07:36.740
to be definitively the difference maker.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:39.530
These are all parts, and that's why it's so
important.

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:42.830
We have a fantastic program coming up for
you today.

